 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail is open at a desktop and shut to its icons on a tablet, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page level is the page the entry belongs to: the entry takes none of its own. A medium entry is a sheet beside its page at a desktop, a third and two thirds of the width, and under its page on a tablet and a phone. Every screen shows the page and the entry, with the same filter bar, the same records and the same fields. On a phone the records are the lines of a list and the boxes of the filter bar stand in two rows. It holds one container: its title and the action that closes it stand in its header, and its actions in its footer. A dialog over its page is not drawn here, because a skeleton lays no frame over another.",
